=== SURVEY ===
Examined web/src/lib/sseManager.ts (143 lines) and web/src/lib/automationSSE.ts (162 lines).

Both files contain:
- fetchSSEToken() function (lines 29-38 in sseManager, 57-66 in automationSSE)
  Calls GET /api/v1/sse-token, returns JWT token string or null
- doConnect() is async, calls fetchSSEToken(), builds URL with ?token= conditional
- sseManager: `/api/v1/events?token=${encodeURIComponent(token)}`
- automationSSE: `/api/v1/automations/events?token=${encodeURIComponent(token)}`

Broader search for fetchSSEToken|sse-token across web/src/ found 0 references outside these two files.

=== REASONING ===
With ForwardAuth middleware in place, the browser automatically sends the auth cookie
on same-domain requests. The SSE token exchange endpoint (/api/v1/sse-token) and the
?token= query parameter are dead code — the EventSource just needs the plain URL.

Changes required:
1. sseManager.ts: Delete fetchSSEToken(), make doConnect() synchronous, use plain '/api/v1/events'
2. automationSSE.ts: Same — delete fetchSSEToken(), synchronous doConnect(), plain '/api/v1/automations/events'
3. automationSSE.ts: Update doc comment that mentions "token-based auth"

